    "skyNote": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "maxH": 620,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Sky options\n\n1 · Night storybook: lighter blue night, gold twinkle stars, the Star of Bethlehem. Most “1999 homepage”.\n2 · Night realistic: deep navy, fine stars, faint Milky Way, the Star. Darkest option.\n3 · Northern lights: soft green and violet glow above the town.\n4 · Dawn: violet to peach, last stars fading, sun glowing behind Bethlehem.\n5 · Daytime (current default): blue sky, sun, clouds; sandstone town. Text on the sky switches to dark ink.\n\nThe town’s stone, shading and lit windows are tuned to each sky. Text on the sky stays at 4.5:1 or better. Wood panels, buttons and the gift tag stay the same in all five.\n\nEvery screen has a “sky” tweak, so any board can be switched.",
      "w": 420,
      "x": 6840,
      "y": 8670
    },
    "tryIt": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "maxH": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Try in Play:\n• Host dashboard: tap “Keep some people apart” to add or remove rules, “Edit” to remove a person, then Draw names. The draw is blocked if rules would force a pair.\n• After the draw: “See who’s opened” and “More options” (cancel & reopen).\n• Mobile “no fair draw”: remove the Alex–Sam rule. Draw turns on, with a warning that 3 people is too few to keep it secret from the host.\n• Gift tag: Unwrap / Hide it again. Long-wishes tag: Show all wishes.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 0
    }
  },
